## Machine Learning

The project investigates two anomaly-detection algorithms:

- Isolation Forest
- Local Outlier Factor (LOF)

The machine-learning section uses separate healthy and unhealthy datasets.

The features used in the analysis include:

```text
time
current
voltage
stress
strain
gx
gy
gz
current_voltage
stress_strain
```

Two additional derived features are created:

```text
current_voltage = current × voltage
stress_strain   = stress × strain
```

Before model training, the features are standardised using `StandardScaler`.

---

## Isolation Forest

Isolation Forest is used to identify observations that differ from the normal structural data.

The implementation performs hyperparameter tuning using `GridSearchCV`.

The parameters explored include:

```text
n_estimators
max_samples
contamination
max_features
```

The model is trained using the healthy dataset and subsequently used to identify anomalous observations in the unhealthy dataset.

The implementation uses:

```text
-1 -> anomaly
 1 -> normal
```

for the Isolation Forest predictions. :chatgpt-content-reference{index="10"}

---

## Local Outlier Factor

Local Outlier Factor is used as a second anomaly-detection method.

The implementation performs parameter tuning for:

```text
n_neighbors
contamination
```

LOF provides an additional method for examining whether individual observations differ from their surrounding data distribution.

Using both methods allows the project to compare different approaches to identifying unusual structural behaviour.

